# De Ashi Harai (Forward Foot Sweep)

> **Source:** Technique Description and Breakdown sourced from *Kodokan Judo*, pg. 60

---

## Technique Description
> "You force your opponent to step forward, then sweep his advancing foot out from under him."

---

## Technique Breakdown
1. Begin in the right natural posture.
2. Step back a bit farther with your right foot and pull your opponent forward. He will take a large step with his left foot.
3. Loosen your right grip a bit and pull him toward you with your left hand so that he brings his right foot up close to his left.
4. Just as he is putting his right foot down, sweep it in the direction it is traveling with your left foot.
5. As you sweep, pull down hard with your left hand.
6. Your opponent will fall, slapping the mat with his left hand and arm.

---

## Technique Overview

| Category | Details |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Hands** | Standard lapel and sleeve grip. Push the sleeve grip in the direction of the throw. |
| **Feet** | Depending on angle of throw, initial step forward or back to force movement. |
| **Timing** | Opponent must be about to place his foot (and weight) onto the mat. |
| **Variations** | There are entry/footwork differences for various angles, but the throw is the same. |

### Combinations
* **As a starting technique:**
  * De Ashi Harai to O Goshi
* **As a finishing technique:**
  * (Circling) Sasae Tsurikomi Ashi to De Ashi Harai
  * O Uchi Gari to De Ashi Harai

### Counters
* **De Ashi Harai (De Ashi Harai)** – Lift foot so opponent misses, then sweep their advanced foot.

